                        "review": "A phenomenal soundtrack, which also happens to come with a good game.\n\nNo, seriously, the music in this game is absolute perfection. Every single track is incredibly catchy and memorable; even the few songs I wasn't sold on initially completely grew on me over time. Every single zone features an instrumental track that transitions into a vocal version during boss fights, with the late-game areas even having multiple tracks. I’ve added almost the entire OST to my own playlist.\n\nAs for the gameplay? It's Darkest Dungeon or X-Com, but with cats. From your home base, you breed new cats, optimizing their stats and skills before embarking on runs. Each cat can only be used once. I found that normal and even hard mode are perfectly manageable. I only lost two or three runs to bad RNG. I think the game is significantly fairer and more forgiving than Isaac.\n\nI recommend this to any fan of tactical RPGs. And even if the genre isn't your thing, do listen to the soundtrack on YouTube.",
